Author: b <a@b>
Date:   Thu Oct 8 10:30:00 2026 -0700

    Fill in the assertions
    
    Every expected value was worked out by hand from the spec, and the
    comments show the arithmetic.
    
    computeGrade multiplies fractions, so its results can be off by a
    tiny amount (82.00000000000001), and those tests use closeTo instead
    of equal. So does the 0.8 GPA.
    
    The error cases pass a function to expect(). Writing
    expect(lms.getLetterGrade(-1)).to.throw() calls getLetterGrade first,
    so it throws before expect() ever sees it, and the test errors out
    instead of passing.
    
    Run the tests: 21 fail, because LMSImpl still says "not implemented".
    But "throws for 11/10" passes. "Not implemented" is an Error too, and
    computeGrade's spec only promises an Error, so the test can't tell
    the right error from any error. getLetterGrade's spec names a
    RangeError, so its tests can be stricter. A vague spec makes for a
    weak test.
    
    lms-coverage has an implementation, and every test passes there.

